WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.360
Do we know what our AI agents
can do on our computers?

00:00:03.795 --> 00:00:07.305
Claude, Codex and Hermes now
come up in the boardroom.

00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:11.280
Five things decide whether they
are a gain or a new way in.

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:15.140
First, the model answers
and the harness acts.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.070
A model takes in text and gives text back.

00:00:18.355 --> 00:00:20.605
The harness is the program around it.

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:25.100
It runs the commands the model asks for,
and decides what needs approval.

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:28.940
So ask which model, which harness,
and where our data goes.

00:00:30.017 --> 00:00:31.927
Second, three words you will hear.

00:00:32.217 --> 00:00:35.127
An agent is a model and
a harness in a loop.

00:00:35.377 --> 00:00:38.567
A skill is a folder of
instructions for one task.

00:00:38.952 --> 00:00:43.762
An MCP server plugs the agent into mail,
tickets or a database.

00:00:44.202 --> 00:00:46.972
Each one adds power,
and a way to misuse it.

00:00:47.983 --> 00:00:50.693
Third and fourth,
skills and servers are software.

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:52.483
Text can hide in a skill.

00:00:52.863 --> 00:00:57.453
Invisible characters show nothing
on screen, yet models can read them.

00:00:57.653 --> 00:00:59.883
Scripts in a skill are run, not read.

00:01:00.228 --> 00:01:02.948
An MCP server often runs on a laptop,

00:01:02.948 --> 00:01:07.358
with the same rights as the
AI application that starts it.

00:01:07.548 --> 00:01:12.778
OWASP puts prompt injection at number
one in its Top 10 for AI applications.

00:01:13.983 --> 00:01:16.013
Fifth, limits outside the model.

00:01:16.283 --> 00:01:20.833
A model can be talked into things,
so safety cannot rest on it saying no.

00:01:21.118 --> 00:01:25.408
The harness runs in a sandbox that
reaches only the project folder.

00:01:25.793 --> 00:01:27.903
Risky actions wait for a person.

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:30.160
What good looks like.

00:01:30.445 --> 00:01:34.375
One approved list of agents,
skills and servers, with an owner.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.170
A person reads every file before install.

00:01:37.535 --> 00:01:39.825
Each server gets its own narrow token.

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:43.540
Agents run in a sandbox,
and every action is logged.

00:01:45.397 --> 00:01:46.607
A suggested first step.

00:01:46.892 --> 00:01:50.642
Ask which AI agents our people use,
and who chose them.

00:01:50.837 --> 00:01:54.307
Then consider one approved list,
with settings fixed centrally.

00:01:55.883 --> 00:01:58.933
Agents are safe because of
limits around the model.

00:01:59.158 --> 00:02:01.448
Approve the harness, not only the model.

